---
// The hero + the single most persuasive object on the page: a rendered product
// surface refusing to guess. No competitor's landing page can show a refusal.
// Copy is v4's plain first-person voice; the headline is fixed.
---

<section id="top" class="grid-atmos relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="shell grid items-center gap-14 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-20 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>

      <h1 class="rise mt-6 text-[clamp(2.5rem,6.2vw,4.6rem)]">
        The health companion that
        <span class="text-accent-soft">refuses to flatter you.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="rise mt-7 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Every other app tells you <span class="text-ink">&ldquo;great job&rdquo;</span> &mdash; even
        when it isn&rsquo;t true. This is the one that won&rsquo;t. It works with a little band you
        wear on your wrist, reads what the band records, and tells you the truth about your body,
        kindly. When it hasn&rsquo;t seen enough of you, it just says
        <span class="text-ink">&ldquo;I don&rsquo;t know yet.&rdquo;</span> No cheering. No fake numbers.
      </p>

      <div class="rise mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="#waitlist" class="btn btn-primary">Join the waitlist</a>
        <a href="#coach" class="btn btn-ghost">See how it answers &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="rise mt-6 max-w-md text-sm text-ink-faint">
        It works with the <span class="text-ink-soft">Amazfit Helio Strap</span> &mdash; a small band
        you buy on your own, from anyone. We don&rsquo;t sell it and we&rsquo;re not part of the
        company that makes it. We just make it honest.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- the refusal, rendered as a flat ledger sheet -->
    <div class="rise lg:justify-self-end">
      <p class="mono mb-3 pl-1 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Most days it has plenty to say. Some days it says this:
      </p>
      <figure
        class="surface surface-lift surface-key w-full max-w-md p-6 sm:p-7"
        aria-label="Rendered example: the product declining to score on insufficient data"
      >
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
            Recovery &middot; today
          </span>
          <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">not enough data</span>
        </figcaption>

        <hr class="hairline my-5" />

        <p class="display-line text-[1.6rem]">
          I don&rsquo;t have enough to score you today. Wear it tonight and I&rsquo;ll know more in
          the morning.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Only <span class="mono text-ink">2</span> of the last
          <span class="mono text-ink">7</span> nights got a clean read on your heart while you slept.
          A score needs a steady picture of your normal &mdash; and a guess would be worse than
          waiting.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="mono text-xs text-ink-faint">last 7 nights</span>
          <span class="cov" aria-hidden="true">
            <i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <span class="chip">read on 2 of 7 nights</span>
          <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">fix&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;wear it 5+ nights</span>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <p class="mono mt-3 pl-1 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        An example of what it says, not a live reading.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- honest status ribbon -->
  <div class="shell">
    <div
      class="rise flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 border-y border-line py-4 text-sm text-ink-soft"
    >
      <span class="eyebrow">Where it stands</span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">live</span> The engine that runs it: built and running
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-dot">building</span> The phone app: being built now
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-dot">closed</span>
        Sign-ups: not open yet &middot;
        <a class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-accent" href="#waitlist">the waitlist is</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
